			<prcStep>
				<stepDesc>Interpolate 8 DEMs [DEM_1-DEM_8] using the ArcGIS Pro Topo to Raster tool with default parameters. Inputs are elevation contours, stream lines, lake polygons, and elevation points. All DEMs uses the same stream, lake, and elevation points, but the elevation contours are varied such that DEM_1 uses Contours_80 supplemented with contours at 16 ft intervals from Contours_2ft, DEM_2 uses a subset Contours_2ft where each contour values is 2 ft greater than the contours used to produce DEM_1, and this pattern is repeated for DEM_3-DEM_8. For example:
If the contours used to create DEM_1 are Elevation (ft) = (0, 16, 32, 48, 64, 80), 
the contours used to create DEM_2 are Elevation (ft) = (2, 18, 34, 50, 66, 82), 
the contours used to create DEM_3 are Elevation (ft) = (4, 20, 36, 52, 68, 84)…,
